# Dr. Denys Dutykh (Mathematics Department, Khalifa University of Science and Technology, Abu Dhabi, UAE)
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this script, please cite this software as given below."
title: "LorenzUPOs: unstable periodic orbits of the Lorenz system by automatic differentiation"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dutykh
    given-names: Denys
    affiliation: "Khalifa University of Science and Technology"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5247-2788"
repository-code: "https://github.com/dutykh/LorenzUPOs"
license: LGPL-3.0-only
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-15"
keywords:
  - lorenz-system
  - unstable-periodic-orbits
  - periodic-orbits
  - chaos
  - dynamical-systems
  - nonlinear-dynamics
  - automatic-differentiation
  - optimization
  - l-bfgs
  - pytorch
  - python
  - research-code
abstract: >-
  Python script that finds unstable periodic orbits of the Lorenz system. A close return of a long chaotic trajectory,
  found with a k-d tree, gives the first guess; the squared distance between the initial point and its image after one
  period, plus a penalty that keeps away from the equilibria, is then minimised over the initial point and the period
  by L-BFGS, with exact gradients from the automatic differentiation of PyTorch through the DOPRI5 integrator of
  torchdiffeq, and the orbit is checked over three periods and plotted on the attractor.
